---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/site.config";

const lastUpdated = "April 29, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for henrickf.com — the personal site of Henrick F."
  noIndex={false}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-20 pb-32">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">
      ← Home
    </a>

    <header class="mt-12 pb-10 border-b border-[color:var(--color-line)]">
      <div class="text-xs text-[color:var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-6">
        Last updated · {lastUpdated}
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl tracking-tight leading-[1.05]">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-xl text-[color:var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        The rules for using this website. Plain language, no surprises.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-essay mt-12 text-lg leading-[1.75]">
      <p>
        This site (<a href={site.url}>henrickf.com</a>) is the personal website of {site.founder}.
        By accessing or using it, you agree to the terms below. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        This is a personal portfolio and writing site. It exists to share work, essays, and contact information.
        Nothing on this site is an offer of employment, a binding proposal, financial advice, legal advice, or a contract,
        unless you and I have signed a separate written agreement that says so.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Content ownership</h2>
      <p>
        All original content on this site (essays, case studies, copy, images, code samples) is the intellectual property of {site.founder}, except where third-party material is clearly attributed.
        You're welcome to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read, share, and link to anything published here.</li>
        <li>Quote short passages with attribution and a link back to the source page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Republish full essays or substantial excerpts without written permission.</li>
        <li>Use any content to train machine learning models without written permission.</li>
        <li>Pass the work off as your own.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The content here is provided as-is. I aim for accuracy and pull from real operating experience, but writing on a fast-moving topic like AI ages quickly.
        Don't make irreversible business, financial, or technical decisions based solely on something you read on this site. Verify, get advice, run your own numbers.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, {site.founder} is not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages
        arising from your use of this site or any content on it. If you choose to act on something you read here and it doesn't work for your situation,
        that's on you, not on me.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Posts and pages may link to third-party sites (sources, references, tools). I don't control those sites and I'm not responsible for their content,
        accuracy, or privacy practices. Linking isn't an endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact and consulting</h2>
      <p>
        If you reach out via the email address on this site to discuss a project, that initial conversation is not a binding engagement.
        Any consulting, build, or advisory work is governed by a separate written agreement signed by both parties.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I may update these terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent revision.
        Continued use of the site after a revision means you accept the new terms.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Mexico, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.
        If you're using the site from another jurisdiction, you're responsible for complying with your local laws.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-20 pt-12 border-t border-[color:var(--color-line)] flex justify-between items-center">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">
        ← Home
      </a>
      <a href="/privacy" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">
        Privacy Policy →
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
